[statement]
A name whose single candidate depends on another requires that name with
the constraint the candidate states: `so:r`'s one candidate `r` needs
`so:n`, whose one candidate `n` needs `lib<2`. `lib`, a name some package
carries, is required with `lib<2` before `n` is installed, and gets 1.0.
Contrast `a-shared-dependency-carries-no-constraint`, where two candidates
share the dependency and `lib` gets 2.0.

[repository]
P:app
V:1
D:so:r

P:r
V:1
p:so:r=1
D:so:n

P:n
V:1
p:so:n=1
D:lib<2

P:lib
V:1.0

P:lib
V:2.0

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install lib 1.0
install n 1
install r 1
install app 1
